{"title":"2014 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 12A Problems\">2014 AMC 12A #22</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 10A Problems\">2014 AMC 10A #25</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f89c2402133dba0ce0d0f5db38c33fd0635466e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{867}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b98ae20267e31e37336bcabc2b5e635591ca0250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2013}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db2db65006422553ef8b4f8531170496bd48b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2014}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" />.  How many pairs of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> are there such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b4d5266ee5ddfa2de9e3d4c35b95a67229ca35e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq m\\leq 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0dd87b90d59f4e58a09e5b2e78b8af6511482d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^n&lt;2^m&lt;2^{m+2}&lt;5^{n+1}?\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/f/b8f65d7dfd34edd356680786e215f513b52cfeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }278\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }279\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }280\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }281\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }282\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Between any two consecutive powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> there are either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593edac1c2e377fbe7df18af5a7aa4813fef3972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2&lt;5^1&lt;2^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />). Consider the intervals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08c68fbf366507bda1d3d539b40c1c434b2517e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5^0,5^1),(5^1,5^2),\\dots (5^{866},5^{867})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"19\" />. We want the number of intervals with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From the given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abeb0a3a887c2871efdca9a6801c1f3037143f44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2013}&lt;5^{867}&lt;2^{2014}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" />, we know that these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e556bd22ea35cf4609d3fc1d7dfc2490fd557d11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$867$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> intervals together have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> of them have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> of them have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus we have the system\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/1580c31f4d58c540f94347ac313ba29d0a32fcda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x+y=867\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b29d4cbbbad5954993ebfc4f5348eb1a5ad481.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x+3y=2013\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />\nfrom which we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/747bd99c6d27ef7b5655789652e7f2cf716379b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=279$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem is asking for between how many consecutive powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are there <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s\n</p><p>There can be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between any two consecutive powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c134ae9d194442eec9a0584ff74fc944ce9251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n+1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>The first power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cfef3a5952e7e3cda7e207e2ab0bffc2f48e8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 5^n$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>The second power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cfef3a5952e7e3cda7e207e2ab0bffc2f48e8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 5^n$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090d69a194f5bc096bc3c48546bc517403d215c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The third power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090d69a194f5bc096bc3c48546bc517403d215c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80ae5979960c1fffcfb2ad37cdb2e5bc9b9580c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cdot 5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that it can be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b216498b4cb64f29f3bfdfa60736dc769f06c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c134ae9d194442eec9a0584ff74fc944ce9251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{n+1}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> or not.\n</p><p>If there are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s between every consecutive powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f89c2402133dba0ce0d0f5db38c33fd0635466e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{867}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/34257d2f84821f0768e84043932e25148abb5e51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$867\\cdot 2 = 1734$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s. However, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> before  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f89c2402133dba0ce0d0f5db38c33fd0635466e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{867}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, meaning the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b656c46831ae39a26b85c04f8632971aad7b2361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013 - 1734 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}279}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"188\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DRJvUMsZtl4&amp;t=4s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DRJvUMsZtl4&amp;t=4s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_10A\" title=\"2014 AMC